  number    = "1-1",
  pages     =  014225,
  abstract  = "Self-organized bistability (SOB) stands as a critical behavior
               for the systems delicately adjusting themselves to the brink of
               bistability, characterized by a first-order transition. Its
               essence lies in the inherent ability of the system to undergo
               enduring shifts between the coexisting states, achieved through
